{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/permutationfeatureimportance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Permutation Feature Importance & Model Diagnostics","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftExplain"}]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Diagnostic Tools","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/PermutationImportance"],"anchor":"Diagnostic-Tools"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/PermutationFeatureImportance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Permutation Feature Importance","type":"text"}]},{"text":" measures how much a trained model’s error increases when a single feature column is randomly shuffled, breaking the relationship between that feature and the target outcome.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"$$\\text{Importance}(f_j) = L(X_{\\text{shuffled}(j)}, y) - L(X, y)$$","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"1. Computing Permutation Importance","type":"heading","anchor":"1-Computing-Permutation-Importance"},{"code":["import SwiftExplain","import SwiftML","","let importance = try await PermutationImportance.compute(","    model: trainedModel,","    features: X_val,","    targets: y_val,","    metric: .meanSquaredError,","    nRepeats: 10",")","","for (idx, score) in importance.enumerated() {","    print(\"Feature \\(idx): Mean drop = \\(score.mean), Std = \\(score.std)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Measure true feature importance by evaluating loss degradation after shuffling feature columns.","type":